  "problem": "What was the exact rate of change of the inflation's value at month $1?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ $%$ per month.",
  "worked_solution": "The function ${f}^{′}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the inflation, applicable in the domain of $f(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of inflation at $x=1$ months is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in inflation was $1\\,%$ per month.",
